diff --git a/docs/profile-image-storage.md b/docs/profile-image-storage.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..74bf1d4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/profile-image-storage.md
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# Deploying Active Storage for profile pictures
+
+New user and organization profile pictures use Active Storage. Its URLs take
+precedence when an attachment exists. Otherwise the application uses the same
+CarrierWave URL (or default picture) as before. No legacy pictures are copied or
+deleted by the migration, and other upload types still use CarrierWave.
+
+1. Run `bin/rails db:migrate` before switching traffic to the new release. Keep the
+   existing `public/uploads` volume or S3 objects and their serving configuration
+   in place.
+2. Configure storage on all web and worker instances. S3 installations reuse the
+   CarrierWave bucket and credentials (`AWS_BUCKET_NAME`, `AWS_ID`, `AWS_SECRET`,
+   and `AWS_UPLOAD_REGION` or `AWS_DEFAULT_REGION`; Forem Cloud uses its existing
+   IAM role). The app needs permission to read, write and delete the new objects,
+   and to list the bucket for cleanup.
+   For file storage, use a persistent, writable `storage/` volume or set
+   `ACTIVE_STORAGE_ROOT` to a persistent directory. It must be shared across
+   web and worker instances. Back it up alongside the database and legacy uploads.
+3. Make sure the application can serve GETs to `/rails/active_storage/blobs/proxy/`
+   through your reverse proxy or CDN. Switch web traffic and workers to the new
+   version before accepting profile-picture writes; the previous version cannot
+   serve these URLs.
+
+Once new uploads have been accepted, a rollback must retain the Active Storage
+read route, tables and storage. Rolling back to code that only reads CarrierWave
+would hide newly uploaded pictures. Keep the Rails signing key stable across deploys
+so previously issued URLs remain valid.
diff --git a/lib/active_storage/service/forem_s3_service.rb b/lib/active_storage/service/forem_s3_service.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..82f2bbd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/lib/active_storage/service/forem_s3_service.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@
+module ActiveStorage
+  class Service
+    # Server-side uploads and proxy reads using Forem's existing Fog S3 client.
+    class ForemS3Service < Service
+      def initialize(bucket:, **credentials)
+        super()
+        @bucket = bucket
+        @storage = Fog::Storage.new(provider: "AWS", **credentials)
+      end
+
+      def upload(key, io, checksum: nil, content_type: nil, **)
+        headers = { "Content-MD5" => checksum, "Content-Type" => content_type }.compact
+        instrument(:upload, key: key, checksum: checksum) { @storage.put_object(@bucket, key, io, headers) }
+      rescue Excon::Error::BadRequest => e
+        raise ActiveStorage::IntegrityError if e.response.body.include?("<Code>BadDigest</Code>")
+
+        raise
+      end
+
+      def download(key)
+        if block_given?
+          instrument(:streaming_download, key: key) do
+            @storage.get_object(@bucket, key) { |chunk, _remaining, _total| yield chunk.b }
+          end
+        else
+          instrument(:download, key: key) { @storage.get_object(@bucket, key).body.b }
+        end
+      rescue Excon::Error::NotFound
+        raise ActiveStorage::FileNotFoundError
+      end
+
+      def download_chunk(key, range)
+        instrument(:download_chunk, key: key, range: range) do
+          @storage.get_object(@bucket, key, "Range" => "bytes=#{range.begin}-#{range.end}").body.b
+        end
+      rescue Excon::Error::NotFound
+        raise ActiveStorage::FileNotFoundError
+      end
+
+      def delete(key)
+        instrument(:delete, key: key) { @storage.delete_object(@bucket, key) }
+      end
+
+      def delete_prefixed(prefix)
+        instrument(:delete_prefixed, prefix: prefix) do
+          @storage.directories.new(key: @bucket).files.all(prefix: prefix).each(&:destroy) # rubocop:disable Rails/FindEach
+        end
+      end
+
+      def exist?(key)
+        instrument(:exist, key: key) do |payload|
+          @storage.head_object(@bucket, key)
+          payload[:exist] = true
+        rescue Excon::Error::NotFound
+          payload[:exist] = false
+        end
+      end
+    end
+  end
+end
